  "period_note": "Solo basis (see reporting_basis note in sources.json). Own contemporaneous annual report: Balance Sheet and Profit & Loss Account (Solo, pp.62-64 area) plus its own 'Five Years Performance of RBL at a Glance' table. CAPITAL DIVERGENCE: this report's own figures (Tier-I 1030.77, Tier-II 244.78, Total capital 1275.55 crore, CRAR 10.16%) are used per the dataset's 'prefer contemporaneous' rule. The FY2016 annual report's later comparative column for FY2013 instead shows Tier-I 430.97, Tier-II 239.43, Total capital 670.40 (implied CRAR ~5.34%) - a large restatement, repeated identically in the FY2017 report's (otherwise badly OCR-garbled) five-year table. Both the FY2013 and FY2016/17 versions are internally self-consistent with their own respective 'Capital excess/(shortfall)' rows (+19.91 vs -585.24), so neither is 'arithmetically impossible'; the earlier, contemporaneous figure is kept per the standing rule and the restated one is recorded here. Classified loans (17,992,507,000 Taka, NPL 16.75%) and required/maintained provision are taken from the FY2014 report's clean (non-OCR) FY2013 comparative column rather than FY2013's own report, because FY2013's own Note 7.09 is an image-scan OCR'd table with visibly incomplete rows that do not reconcile to its own printed subtotals. EPS (1.93) and NAVPS (65.12) are the FY2014 report's restated FY2013 comparatives (computed off FY2014's enlarged bonus-adjusted share count per BAS 33); FY2013's own report shows ambiguous/OCR-corrupted EPS figures that could not be reliably read.",
